License: GPL-2
Comment: keyboard-en.lst is Tux Typing's own table of which finger types each
 key, as Debian's tuxtype-data installs it, with each key's place on the US
 keyboard added; keyboard-es.lst is the same for the Spanish keyboard, with
 the ñ, the comma, the full stop, the hyphen and the accented vowels.

